                <pb facs="1185" n="1173" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg1173"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.51/939: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-13T17:00:00-03:00">December 13, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>304. Your 159, December 12, 8 p.m. I have advised both Costa and Charlone of the
                    information regarding the credits.</p>
                <p>Charlone was disappointed that no approval has yet been given to the request for
                    $5,000,000 for national defense. He asked that Pierson be informed that he
                    attaches vastly more importance to the credit for <pb facs="1186" n="1174"
                        xml:id="pg1174"/> this purpose (for as long term as possible) than to the
                    other credits and that he hopes affirmative action on this request will be taken
                    soon. I should appreciate receiving any information available in this
                    connection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
